cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TEMPUS: Relativistic coordinate time scales for any solar-system body from arbitrary ephemerides"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Seyffert
    given-names: Yan
  - family-names: Fienga
    given-names: Agnès
abstract: >-
  TEMPUS computes relativistic time-coordinate offsets (e.g. TCX-TCB) by
  numerically integrating the post-Newtonian time-transformation along a target body's
  ephemeris-defined worldline. It is ephemeris-agnostic via use of CALCEPH
  (JPL/INPOP/EPM) and can produce Chebyshev products.
keywords:
  - time scale
  - reference systems
  - ephemerides
  - celestial mechanics
license: BSD-3-Clause
version: 1.0.0